    ('shelf: Berakhot 20b — the_persons', lambda: the_good_land({'ask': 'the_persons'}, DATA), "the grace's persons (8:10) — women obligated, by the Torah or the Sages OPEN (Berakhot 20b:1, 20b:11-14; a woman blesses for her husband under the Sages' curse, 20b:12); the priests at the atonement meal form the invitation (Arakhin 4a); consecrated food needs the blessing (Bava Metzia 114a); the minor blesses for a father who ate without satisfaction (20b:14): the woman at the table holds, the level open"),
    ('shelf: Berakhot 44a:10, 35b:20 — the_meals_base', lambda: the_good_land({'ask': 'the_meals_base'}, DATA), "the meal's base (8:10) — 'a land in which you shall eat BREAD' (8:9) concluded the matter: the grace's object bread (Berakhot 44a:10 the Rabbis; the seven species one blessing abridged from three, 44a:12); no meal is based on wine — the one who based his on wine says no full grace (35b:20-21); whatever satiates and a meal is based on requires it — 'that is hunger' (42a:2): the wine-based meal EXEMPT from the full grace"),
